    {
      "index": 4,
      "className": "csp-story",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "THE SITUATION"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A medical centre in Dublin with several GPs, a reception team under pressure and a website that listed opening hours and little else."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Patients phoned for everything because the site offered nothing else. Load time was over two seconds on a phone, the booking link was buried, and new patients could not tell if the practice was taking registrations."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "WHAT WE CHANGED"
        },
        {
          "type": "ol",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A new accessible site built around three tasks: book, register, find information",
              "href": null,
              "imgs": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Online booking on every page, with clear rules for who can book what",
              "href": null,
              "imgs": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Service pages for vaccinations, screening and chronic care, written in plain language",
              "href": null,
              "imgs": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Google Business Profile with services, hours and booking link",
              "href": null,
              "imgs": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Tracking of bookings, registrations and calls so the practice could see the shift",
              "href": null,
              "imgs": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "WHAT HAPPENED"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Within six months 58% of appointments were booked online, calls to reception fell by a third and the site loads in under a second."
        }
      ]
    },
